  "limitations": "1. Record length: 20 years (2005-2024) for 5 regions. WMO climatological normals use 30 years. Each region-month has about 19 to 20 values before pooling.\n2. Regional aggregation: values are averages over large macro-regions and smooth out local extremes.\n3. Precipitation unit: UNCONFIRMED. Regional values run from 0.00 to 30.95. Results are reported in relative (log-scale) terms.\n4. Warming drift: training base rate for temperature is 9.6%. Detrended base rate drift (test minus train) is +12.1 points; fixed-mode drift is +25.1 points.\n5. Degenerate dry-season months: 11 region-month pairs excluded in the final window. Excluded test rows: 32 of 175.\n6. Test section not executed in this run (lock present). Test figures come from the original sealed run.\n9. Outputs are relative risk tiers, not disaster or weather forecasts. External drivers (ENSO/IOD) were not used because the files were not provided."
